WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.313
Most coexistence outages
are revocation outages.

2
00:00:03.313 --> 00:00:08.581
Relying parties now sit in three places,
inside the network, on the internet,

3
00:00:08.581 --> 00:00:11.980
and in Entra ID, and each
CA's CRL must be reachable

4
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:15.974
from all three wherever its
certificates are validated.

5
00:00:15.974 --> 00:00:22.625
Every relying party that validates Cloud
PKI certificates, including on-premises

6
00:00:22.625 --> 00:00:28.600
RADIUS and VPN servers, needs outbound
HTTP to the Intune-hosted CDP and AIA.

7
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:34.740
A BYOCA issuing CA's own CRL is
Intune-hosted too, but its parent CRL and

8
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:40.987
AIA come from the private CA, and AD
CS defaults to an LDAP AIA location.

9
00:00:40.987 --> 00:00:48.206
AD CS CAs that issue user certificates for
Entra CBA usually publish over LDAP plus

10
00:00:48.206 --> 00:00:54.290
an internal HTTP URL; Entra ID needs
one internet HTTP or HTTPS URL per CA,

11
00:00:54.290 --> 00:01:00.375
HTTP recommended, with no OCSP and no
LDAP, and watch the CRL size limits,

12
00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:06.975
twenty megabytes for commercial and GCC
and forty-five for Azure Government.

13
00:01:06.975 --> 00:01:11.938
And the CAs behind domain controller
certificates must serve Entra-joined devices

14
00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:16.475
that haven't authenticated yet, so
LDAP-only distribution points break them.

15
00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:20.450
Fixing an AD CS distribution
point means two things.

16
00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:27.325
Add an HTTP location reachable from the
internet, using HTTP rather than HTTPS.

17
00:01:27.325 --> 00:01:32.850
And recognize that the new URL appears only
in certificates issued after the change.

18
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:36.546
Entra ID uses the CRL URL
configured in its trust store,

19
00:01:36.546 --> 00:01:39.009
not the one inside each certificate,

20
00:01:39.009 --> 00:01:43.444
so CBA works as soon as the trust
store points at the published CRL;

21
00:01:43.444 --> 00:01:48.125
other relying parties keep failing
until their certificates renew.

22
00:01:48.125 --> 00:01:53.766
The program publishes on plain anonymous
HTTP, not through an application proxy,

23
00:01:53.766 --> 00:01:59.640
because Entra ID must download the CRL
without authentication within ten seconds.
